  "body": "## What changed\n\nPart of #372 (decision: the machine's axis really moves the other way; the CAM side stays right-handed). This builds on #385 (merged), which added the per-axis `direction`. #385 refused posting for any inverted axis. This PR replaces that refusal with a translation, plus named refusals for what is not verified.\n\n- **One place: the engine** (`crates/post/src/post/invert.rs`, called from `engine::run_numbered_with` before any hook). The record stream is mirrored into the controller's frame, so every script sees the controller's coordinates. No script grows sign logic. A standard machine gets its records back untouched.\n- **How the machine reaches it:** `machine::mirror` writes `\"invertedAxes\": [...]`, but only when some axis is inverted, so standard mirrors stay byte-identical. Through the raw door (a `.mch` file's own JSON, the CLI's `--machine`), the engine re-reads `\"direction\"` with `parse_mch`.\n- **Which scripts may post it:** a new manifest flag, `axisInversion = true`, set in `fanuc.cps` and `haas.cps` only. It is documented in `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`.\n- The app's verification gate and the CLI keep `Machine::inverted_post_refusal()`. It now refuses only what the post cannot translate (Z or any other letter). The machine editor's note now says \"posted mirrored: Fanuc / Haas posts only\" for X/Y and \"posting refused for this axis\" for anything else.\n- Decisions are in `docs/decisions/374-inverted-axis-post.md`.\n\n## Translation rules (for each inverted X / Y)\n\n1. That axis's coordinates get the opposite sign. This covers move and cycle end points, arc centres (so I for X and J for Y flip with them), the `StartX/Y` chain and the work-offset origin (`OriginX/Y`). The stock box edges negate and swap (left <-> right, front <-> back).\n2. An arc in a plane that contains exactly one inverted axis reverses sense: CW <-> CCW, so G2 <-> G3. Two inverted axes in the same plane cancel.\n3. XY cutter compensation swaps sides (G41 <-> G42) when exactly one of X and Y is inverted.\n\n## Refused by name\n\nThese are hard `PostError::Refused` errors and nothing is posted. They are not counted warnings, because the CLI writes its output file even when there are warnings. Each refusal is listed once per run.\n\n- An inverted **Z** (\"tool-length compensation (G43) and the canned cycles' retract assume the controller's +Z leaves the work\"), or any letter other than X / Y.\n- Any post script without `axisInversion = true`: Sinumerik, Heidenhain, Mazak, Tormach, Fanuc Lathe, and user scripts.\n- Helical arcs, threading cycles, tilted (A/B/C rotary) moves, C-axis live tooling (polar / G12.1).\n- Probing (TOUCH/RETREAT/FOUND). Follow-up: #392.\n- A stock box edge without its pair.\n- A static-grammar axis stating `\"reversal\": true`. Before this PR that key was silently ignored.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/inverted_equivalence.rs`:\n  - `an_inverted_machine_cuts_the_cam_path` is **the key safety test**. A small RS-274 reader interprets the posted Fanuc and Haas programs as a controller whose axes are inverted (X, Y, and X+Y). It maps the motion back through the work offset and compares it with the CAM path: lines, G2/G3 in G17/G18/G19 with I/J/K, the drilled hole, and the physical comp side. Tolerance is 0.002 mm.\n  - `the_standard_program_on_an_inverted_machine_strays` is the converse: the untranslated program fails the same reader, so the reader is not a tautology.\n- `crates/app/tests/inverted_post.rs` (15 tests):\n  - Goldens: `inverted_x_goldens_for_fanuc_and_haas` (`golden/nc/inverted/{fanuc,haas}_x.nc`) and `the_inverted_x_golden_carries_the_translated_words`.\n  - Standard machines untouched: `a_standard_machine_posts_byte_identical`, `the_mirror_states_the_inverted_axes_only_when_there_are_any`.\n  - Translation of params: `the_stock_box_and_origin_mirror`, `the_raw_door_reads_a_files_direction`.\n  - One test per refusal: `a_helical_arc_refuses_by_name`, `a_tilted_move_refuses_by_name`, `live_tooling_refuses_by_name`, `a_threading_cycle_refuses_by_name`, `probing_refuses_by_name`, `every_refusal_is_named_once_in_one_run`, `an_inverted_z_or_other_letter_refuses_by_name`, `every_unverified_dialect_refuses_by_name`, `an_unread_machine_word_refuses_by_name`.\n- `crates/app/tests/axis_direction.rs`: the two #385 refusal tests are replaced by `an_inverted_x_machine_posts_the_mirrored_program` (a real document posts through `post_setup`; every X/I word is negated and G2/G3 swapped against the standard post), `an_inverted_z_refuses_posting_by_name` and `the_refusal_names_every_inverted_axis`.\n- `crates/post/tests/axis_direction_cli.rs`: `the_cli_posts_an_inverted_x_mirrored`, `the_cli_refuses_an_inverted_z_by_name`, `the_cli_refuses_an_unverified_script_for_an_inverted_x`.\n\n## Gate (quick, debug, this worktree, after merging origin/main)\n\n- app suites, all green: axis_direction 12, inverted_post 15, inverted_equivalence 2, posting 17, conformance 6, golden_cl 23, fanuc_post 8, machine 32, control_comp 5, wear_comp 5, arc_planes 8, c_axis_live 4, heidenhain_arc_centre 2, heidenhain_block_form 4, lathe_post 7, lathe_post_g76 5, lathe_post_refusals 5, probe_op 11, scripting 17, tormach_machines 5.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`, all green: post_engine 33, comp 9, axis_direction_cli 3.\n- None of the existing goldens changed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nNot exercised: the machine editor's new note (the GUI was not launched), and any real controller.\n\nFound on the way: #391. Fanuc/Haas engage G41/G42 while a G18/G19 plane is still modal. This is not specific to inversion; the probe stream steps back to G17 before its COMP so the goldens do not lock that behaviour.\n\nChangelog: A machine with an inverted X and/or Y axis now posts through the Fanuc and Haas posts. The program is mirrored for the controller: the axis's coordinates and I/J/K are negated, G2/G3 and G41/G42 swap where exactly one inverted axis is in the plane, and the work-offset origin is negated. An inverted Z, helical arcs, threading, rotary/tilted moves, live tooling, probing and every other post are refused by name.\n\nFixes #374\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
